{"slug":"rotated-string","title":"Rotated String","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":125,"tags":["strings","rotation","substring"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Doubling a string shows all its rotations","body":["A rotation moves some letters from the front to the back: `abcde` can become `cdeab`. If you write the word twice, `abcdeabcde`, then every rotation of the word appears in it as a block of the same length.",{"code":"is_rotation = len(s) == len(t) and t in s + s"},"The length check matters: without it `t = \"cd\"` would be found inside `abcdeabcde` although `cd` is not a rotation of `abcde`."]},"statement":["Print `yes` if the word `t` can be obtained from the word `s` by moving some letters from the front of `s` to its back (zero letters is allowed), otherwise print `no`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `s`.","The second line has `t`."],"outputFormat":["Print `yes` or `no`."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s, t <= 5000","The words contain lowercase letters."],"examples":[{"input":"abcde\ncdeab\n","output":"yes\n","note":"Move ab to the back."},{"input":"abcde\nabced\n","output":"no\n","note":"Not a rotation."}],"hints":["A rotation must have the same length as the original.","Write the word twice: all rotations are inside `s + s`.","Check that `t` occurs in `s + s`."],"starter":{"python":"s = input().strip()\nt = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n        String t = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Every rotation of `s` is a block of `s + s` with the length of `s`. So `t` is a rotation exactly when the lengths agree and `t` occurs in `s + s`."],"complexity":"Time O(n) to O(n * m) depending on the search used, space O(n).","code":{"python":"s = input().strip()\nt = input().strip()\n\nprint(\"yes\" if len(s) == len(t) and t in s + s else \"no\")\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n\n    bool ok = s.size() == t.size() && (s + s).find(t) != string::npos;\n    cout << (ok ? \"yes\" : \"no\") << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n        String t = sc.next();\n\n        boolean ok = s.length() == t.length() && (s + s).contains(t);\n        System.out.println(ok ? \"yes\" : \"no\");\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"abcde\ncdeab\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"abcde\nabced\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"ab\nba\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"abc\nab\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"abcde\ncd\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"aab\naba\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"yes\n"}]}